                <pb facs="0418" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg348"/>

                <head>No. 181.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sargent to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 8,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Sargent telegraphs that he immediately presented the request of the
                    President, and that while Bundesrath’s action was adverse, he again protested
                    strongly; asked an answer to the President’s proposal and suspension of
                    action.</p>
            </div>
